                        "options": [
                          "Grace stays on board.",
                          "They move to New York.",
                          "Lucía closes the Madrid office."
                        ],
                        "answer": 0
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "phase": "grammar",
                  "type": "grammar_rule",
                  "content": {
                    "tag": "emphasis",
                    "title": "Emphasis: do, such, so and fronting",
                    "explanation": "Recursos para dar énfasis:\n- «do», «does» o «did» + verbo en afirmativa, para insistir o contrastar: «I do know that market very well.», «We did prepare carefully.»\n- «such (a / an)» + adjetivo + nombre: «such a small studio», «such ambitious plans»\n- «so» + adjetivo o adverbio; con resultado, «so» / «such… that…»: «so convincing»\n- Inversión formal: «So» + adjetivo + «be» + sujeto + «that»: «So convincing were your numbers that…»\n- Anteposición (fronting): poner delante lo que queremos destacar: «That we can promise.», «Madrid is where I started.»",
                    "table": {
                      "headers": [
                        "Recurso",
                        "Ejemplo"
                      ],
                      "rows": [
                        [
                          "do / does / did enfático",
                          "I do have to say, that was impressive."
                        ],
                        [
                          "such (a) + adjetivo + nombre",
                          "such a small studio, such ambitious plans"
                        ],
                        [
                          "so + adjetivo",
                          "The plan is so ambitious."
                        ],
                        [
                          "so / such… that",
                          "The numbers were so convincing that he stopped taking notes."
                        ],
                        [
                          "So + adjetivo + verbo + sujeto (formal)",
                          "So convincing were your numbers that…"
                        ],
                        [
                          "anteposición (fronting)",
                          "That we can promise."
                        ]
                      ]
                    },
                    "examples": [
                      "I do have to say, that was impressive.",
                      "Such a small studio, and yet such ambitious plans.",
                      "So convincing were your numbers that my finance director stopped taking notes.",
                      "That we can promise."
                    ]
                  }
                },
